  The reel_script and caption say the 55 students took part in the launch, but the article only says the 55 government school students contributed to the initiative; the article says the device was made by students of the Govt middle school, which is fine, but the caption and script say the 'mini satellite' was launched by students 'in Coimbatore' generally while the article specifies Thudiyalur Corporation Middle School; minor, see next item.
  The reel_script states the 55 students 'took part', which is supported by 'contribution', so no issue there; however the reel_script omits the key fact that the instrument was made by Coimbatore government school students collectively from the article's lead, while the draft attributes making it only to Thudiyalur Corporation middle school students, which is not stated in the article (the article says students of a government middle school in Coimbatore and launched from Thudiyalur Corporation middle school).
  The slides_spec loc field 'துடியலூர், கோவை' and the reel_script 'துடியலூர் மாநகராட்சி நடுநிலைப் பள்ளி மாணவர்கள் இதனை உருவாக்கினர்' attribute both building and launching to the Thudiyalur school, a combination of two facts the article presents separately (the students are from a government middle school; the launch was from Thudiyalur Corporation middle school).
  The caption states 'இந்த அறிவியல் திறமையைப் பார்த்து' and the reel_script omits the article's concluding claim that the students' dream may reach new heights in India's space research; this is editorial framing rather than a factual claim, so not flagged.
